      "value": "VRCSDK3-WORLD-2020.12.09.04.44_Public\nUdonSharp_v0.19.0\nI had tested like this code:\n```\n    public override void OnDrop()\n    {\n        VRC_Pickup pickup = (VRC_Pickup)this.GetComponent(typeof(VRC_Pickup));\n        if (!pickup) { return; }\n        Debug.Log(\"IsHeld[\" + pickup.IsHeld.ToString() + \"]\");\n        Debug.Log(\"Dropped[\" + pickup.name + \"]\");\n        VRC_Pickup left = Networking.LocalPlayer.GetPickupInHand(VRC_Pickup.PickupHand.Left);\n        VRC_Pickup right = Networking.LocalPlayer.GetPickupInHand(VRC_Pickup.PickupHand.Right);\n        Debug.Log(\"LeftHand[\" + ((left) ? left.name : \"null\"));\n        Debug.Log(\"RightHand[\" + ((right) ? right.name : \"null\"));\n.........\n```\nWhen I dropped pickup, logged like this:\n```\n2021.01.05 09:58:34 Log        -  [VRCHandGrasper] Pickup object: 'Chips (2)' equipped = False, is equippable = False, last input method = Oculus, is auto equip controller = False\n2021.01.05 09:58:35 Log        -  [VRCHandGrasper] Drop object: 'Chips (2), was equipped = False' Grab button released, last input method = Oculus\n2021.01.05 09:58:35 Log        -  isHeld[False]\n2021.01.05 09:58:35 Log        -  Dropped[Chips (2)]\n2021.01.05 09:58:35 Log        -  LeftHand[Chips (2)\n2021.01.05 09:58:35 Log        -  RightHand[null\n```",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-05T02:20:04.802Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "On the condition, I attached VRC_PickUp and UdonBehaviour to a single GameObject.\nI want to detect a moment when I drop this pickup object using its Udon.\nSo I checked those 2 values in OnDrop(), but:\n- VRC_PickUp.IsHeld always returns false. Even when I just swapped the pickup to another hand.\n- VRCPlayerApi.GetPickupInHand with an argument which the hand I held the pickup returns an instance what I dropped.\nI think it depends on the VRChat specification whether IsHeld returns false even though I have the pickup, or whether the instance is returned even though I don't have the pickup, which is the correct interpretation, but in any case I feel there is a inconsistency here.\nWhat is the correct interpretation of OnDrop? And I would like these 2 values to be consistent.",
